enchilada: panel brightness and sleep over MIPI DSI; AppleARMBacklight for CoreBrightness

iOS 16.7.16 (iPhone10,3) brightness never goes through an IOMobileFramebuffer selector. CoreBrightness (in backboardd) matches {backlight-control = true}, requires IOObjectConformsTo "AppleARMBacklight" (-[CBDisplayContaineriOS findBacklight] 0x1af0cb224/0x1af0cb398, setupInternalModules 0x1af0cec70) and reads IODisplayParameters/brightness/{value,min,max} (DisplayCreateWithID 0x1af0d8794; without it no display); with none: "Built in display/backlight driver has not been found." and no slider or auto-brightness. With new-backlight-architecture = true it sets "brightness-nits" (SInt32, 16.16 nits; SetBLDriverNitsValue ~0x1aeff5a74) on that service and "IOMFBBrightnessLevel" (same value) on the IOMFB service (SetIOMFBBrightness 0x1af016814). Without backlight-calibration-parameters its range is 5..400 nits (0x1af0d9684).

AppleARMBacklight (child of AppleCLCD) now carries those properties and maps brightness-nits linearly onto the panel's DCS 0x51 range 0..1023, big-endian (panel-samsung-sofef00.c, mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large), with sweetbl_nits (default 400) as the top; the legacy "brightness" key is taken as is, other keys are accepted. AppleCLCD accepts IOMFBBrightnessLevel. RequestPowerChange(0) (selector 12) now also puts the panel to sleep: ABL's pipe back (0254's restore), the splash PINGPONG's autorefresh stopped as dpu_hw_pingpong.c dpu_hw_pp_disable_autorefresh, then 0x28, 40 ms, 0x10, 160 ms (sofef00_panel_off); on: 0x11, 10 ms, 0x29 (sofef00_panel_on without reset/init), autorefresh back and a CTL_START kickoff (dpu_hw_ctl_trigger_start). The software blanking stays.

DCS writes go out through DSI0's command DMA (0xae94000 + DSI_6G_REG_SHIFT 4, v2.2.1) as Linux dsi_host.c does: packet in MSM order (header 1, 2, 0, 0x80 | long 0x40, payload, 0xff pad) in a contiguous buffer below 4 GiB (needs 0250's MDP SMMU bypass verdict: Linux maps it in the MDP address space), CMD_DMA_CTRL = FROM_FRAME_BUFFER | LOW_POWER, CTRL |= CMD_MODE_EN | ENABLE, INTR_CTRL |= MASK_CMD_DMA_DONE, DMA_BASE, DMA_LEN, TRIG_DMA = 1, then CMD_DMA_DONE polled for up to 200 ms and everything put back. TRIG_CTRL gets the software DMA trigger and BLOCK_DMA_WITHIN_FRAME (dsi_ctrl_enable). A timeout stops all further DSI commands for the boot. Each command is logged ("SWEET BL: ..."; brightness at most once a second). fMdpLock serialises it with the MDP. Boot-arg sweetbl=0 turns it all off.

